    <description>The Navigation Camera (NavCam) was a part of the Attitude and Orbital Control System for the Rosetta Orbiter. It comprised two identical CCD cameras to provide for complete redundancy and single event upset. The purpose of the NavCam system was to provide imaging, autonomous acquisition and tracking of star-fields and extended sources, and autonomous navigation for Rosetta.</description>
